h Made, and GlenOaks Farms brand names, as well as under private labels on behalf of customers primarily through direct sales force, brokers, and distributors. Lifeway Foods, Inc. was incorporated in 1986 and is based in Morton Grove, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Julie  Smolyansky | Chairperson of the Board, CEO, President & Secretary | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 293 people. Revenue per employee of $725K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Lifeway Foods, Inc. is a micro-cap consumer defensive business with a $290M market cap on $212M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 10% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The company is burning through $16M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 34% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 127% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation 