y.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Defensive peers: P/E 39.9 vs 17.5 and EV/EBITDA 19.3 vs 10.0 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 19% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -5.7% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $31.67 on average, 65% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 17% clears the cost of capital of 9.6% by 7pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.01).","It runs a 26% gross margin and burns cash (FCF margin -8%).","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only 0.79x.","ROE of 16% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.2x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 12.7, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.23).","The Beneish M-score (-2.13) sits just under the manipulation line, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 14.5% over 3 years, 15.8% over 5 years and 4.5% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 13%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 16.8% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Capex runs 6.9x depreciation (12.9% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 7, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 34.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 57%.","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 15 sales over the past year, net $3.9M sold.","Short interest is elevated at 12.3% of the float, 6.1 days to cover."],"people":["With about 293 employees, each generates about $725K of revenue, 1.4x the Consumer Defensive median, and revenue has grown 8.3% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$56K per employee.","CEO pay is $2.6M (4x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $7K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":59,"head":"Avoid: priced 127% above its fair value of $8.45.","pros":["Composite 48, above the 39 line (gates 14/26)","ROIC 16.8% vs WACC 9.6%","Revenue grew 15.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.3x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 127% above fair value of $8.45","FCF margin 7.7% (burns cash)","P/E 39.9x vs sector 17.5x","EV/EBITDA 19.3x vs sector 10.0x","Heavy insider selling ($3.9M net over 12 months)"],"flags":["Priced 127% above its fair value of $8.45"],"need":[],"buy_below":7.19,"vc":{"base":8.45,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":8.45,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.5059,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (51% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":17.5447,"ev_ebitda":10.0,"pfcf":15.3688,"pb":1.9293,"roic":0.1206,"gross_margin":0.3381,"fcf_margin":0.0601,"div_yield":0.0311}},"ticker":"LWAY","date":"2026-11-20"}